<%- include('partials/header') %>

<!-- Top Hero Banner (Compact & Animated with 2 AM Study - Matches Music, Blog, About, & Terms) -->
<section class="hero-privacy-section">
  <div class="container text-center">
    <div class="hero-privacy-badge">
      <span class="pulse-dot"></span>
      <span>Privacy &amp; Data Protection</span>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield text-primary ms-1" style="font-size: 0.85rem;"></i>
    </div>
    
    <h1 class="animated-2am-title">
      Privacy Policy — <span class="gradient-2am-text">2 AM Study</span>
    </h1>
    
    <p class="hero-privacy-subtitle">
      Learn how we protect student data, respect your privacy rights, and keep your late-night study hub secure.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
/* Hero Section & Animations (Matches Music & Blog Page Hero) */
@keyframes gradientShift {
  0% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
  50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }
  100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
}

@keyframes pulseGlow {
  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 0.8; }
  50% { transform: scale(1.2); opacity: 1; box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.7); }
}

.hero-privacy-section {
  padding: 85px 16px 24px !important;
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.08) 0%, transparent 65%), #f8fafc;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
}

.hero-privacy-badge {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  background: #ffffff;
  border: 1px solid rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.2);
  box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.08);
  border-radius: 50px;
  padding: 5px 14px;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #1e40af;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.pulse-dot {
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: #2563eb;
  animation: pulseGlow 1.8s infinite ease-in-out;
}

.animated-2am-title {
  font-size: 2.2rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: #0f172a;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}

.gradient-2am-text {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2563eb 0%, #7c3aed 45%, #ec4899 75%, #2563eb 100%);
  background-size: 300% 300%;
  -webkit-background-clip: text;
  background-clip: text;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
  animation: gradientShift 5s ease infinite;
}

.hero-privacy-subtitle {
  font-size: 0.92rem;
  color: #64748b;
  max-width: 640px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .animated-2am-title {
    font-size: 1.65rem;
  }
}

.privacy-card {
  background: #ffffff;
  border: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
  border-radius: 20px;
  padding: 2.5rem;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.04);
}

.privacy-section-title {
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #0f172a;
  margin-top: 2rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
  border-bottom: 2px solid #f1f5f9;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}
</style>

<main class="container py-5 my-0">
  <div class="privacy-card">
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center mb-4 pb-3 border-bottom">
      <div>
        <span class="badge bg-primary bg-opacity-10 text-primary px-3 py-1.5 rounded-pill fw-semibold mb-1">Student Privacy Guarantee</span>
        <h2 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-0">Data Privacy &amp; Trust Statement</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="text-muted small mt-2 mt-md-0">
        <i class="fa-regular fa-clock me-1 text-primary"></i> Last updated: <span id="current-date" class="fw-semibold text-dark"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-content lh-lg text-secondary" style="font-size: 0.96rem;">
      <p class="lead text-dark fw-normal mb-4">
        At <strong>2 AM Study</strong>, accessible from our web platform, student trust and data privacy are our highest priorities. This Privacy Policy outlines what information is collected, how it is secured, and how your privacy rights are strictly safeguarded.
      </p>

      <div class="p-3 bg-light rounded-3 mb-4 border-start border-4 border-primary">
        <p class="mb-0 text-dark small">
          If you have any questions regarding your personal information, study records, or account deletion, please reach out to our privacy desk directly at <a href="mailto:2amstudyofficial@gmail.com" class="text-primary fw-bold text-decoration-none">2amstudyofficial@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="privacy-section-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-server text-primary"></i> 1. Log Files &amp; Operational Telemetry</h3>
      <p>Like standard modern web applications, 2 AM Study follows standard logging practices. Information collected in logs includes Internet Protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, device information, timestamp data, and referring pages. These logs are strictly aggregated for diagnostic monitoring, performance optimization, and preventing security abuse.</p>

      <h3 class="privacy-section-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-cookie-bite text-warning"></i> 2. Cookies &amp; Local Storage</h3>
      <p>We use essential cookies and browser storage (such as HTML5 LocalStorage) to preserve your preferences—including Pomodoro timer layouts, sound volume levels, focus streaks, and active study session parameters—so you can seamlessly resume your study workflow across tabs.</p>

      <h3 class="privacy-section-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-gear text-info"></i> 3. CCPA Privacy Rights (Do Not Sell My Personal Information)</h3>
      <p class="fw-semibold text-dark mb-2">Under the CCPA, students and consumers have the following rights:</p>
      <ul class="mb-3 ps-4">
        <li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> Request disclosure of categories and specific pieces of personal data collected.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Deletion:</strong> Request full deletion of all personal data held about your account.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Opt-Out:</strong> We do <strong>not</strong> sell student personal information under any circumstances.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you submit a data request, our compliance team will fulfill your request within 30 days.</p>

      <h3 class="privacy-section-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved text-success"></i> 4. GDPR Data Protection Rights</h3>
      <p class="fw-semibold text-dark mb-2">Every student using 2 AM Study is entitled to full international data protection rights:</p>
      <ul class="mb-3 ps-4">
        <li><strong>Right to Access:</strong> Request digital copies of your profile and data records.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> Request correction of incomplete or outdated profile information.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> Request permanent removal of your account data ("Right to be Forgotten").</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Restrict &amp; Object:</strong> Object to specific automated processing workflows.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Data Portability:</strong> Request export of your study data in a machine-readable format.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="privacy-section-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-child-reaching text-danger"></i> 5. Children's Online Privacy Protection</h3>
      <p>2 AM Study does not knowingly collect Personally Identifiable Information from individuals under the age of 13. If you believe a minor has submitted personal details through our platform, please contact us immediately and we will promptly purge the information from our systems.</p>

      <h3 class="privacy-section-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-handshake-angle text-primary"></i> 6. User Consent &amp; Updates</h3>
      <p>By using the 2 AM Study platform and study tools, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to its provisions. Any policy modifications will be published here with an updated timestamp.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<script>
  document.getElementById('current-date').textContent = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });
</script>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>